86:/// Falls back to the fully lexical [path] when nothing up to the
87:/// filesystem root can be resolved (e.g. a symlink loop — `realpath(3)`
88:/// fails the same way). Public so the planned-path/symlink semantics are
89:/// testable portably, the same way [pathIsWithin] exposes the
90:/// separator-sensitive containment for Windows tests.
91:String canonicalizePath(String path) {
92:  final trail = <String>[];
93:  var current = path;
94:  while (true) {
95:    try {
96:      final head = Directory(current).resolveSymbolicLinksSync();
97:      return trail.isEmpty
98:          ? head
99:          : p.normalize(p.joinAll([head, ...trail.reversed]));
100:    } catch (_) {
101:      final parent = p.dirname(current);
102:      if (parent == current) return path;
103:      trail.add(p.basename(current));
104:      current = parent;
105:    }
106:  }
107:}
